// A name in a pattern that some visible constructor has is that
// constructor, whatever type is matched: it never quietly becomes a binder,
// so importing a file cannot change what a pattern means. The error says
// how to bind instead.
@ cases.a-binder-named-like-a-constructor-is-refused-with-a-hint
files."a.taut" = ```tauto
pub(open) inductive Item: Type {
  Cert(n: Nat, m: Nat): Item
}
```
files."main.nib" = ```tauto
import "a.taut"
fn first(xs: List(Nat)): Nat {
  ⊢ Nat from match xs {
    Nil => 0
    Cons(Cert, rest) => Cert
  }
}
fn first_(xs: List(Nat)): Nat {
  ⊢ Nat from match xs {
    Nil => 0
    Cons(cert_, rest) => cert_
  }
}
```
checks.first = "error: `Item::Cert` is a constructor of `Item`, not `Nat`; a name in a pattern that is a constructor matches that constructor, so to bind the value write a name that is not one, like `cert_`"
checks.first_ = "ok"

// A pattern's head that is no constructor is refused at that pattern, with
